{"name":"Lovely Lavender","hex":"#d6d2dd","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"lovely","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Delightful for beauty, harmony, or grace.","Nice; wonderful."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An attractive, lovely person, especially a (professional) beauty.","Term of fond address."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lovely"},{"term":"lavender","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of a group of European plants, genus, Lavandula, of the mint family.","A pale bluish purple or violet colour, like that of the lavender flower."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a pale purple colour.","Pertaining to LGBT people and rights."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lavender"}],"entries":[{"title":"Lovely (perfume)","blocks":[{"text":"Lovely is a 2005 perfume released by Sarah Jessica Parker. Parker’s first fragrance, Lovely is a light floral musk based on a blend Parker had made for herself. The perfume’s formal development was the subject of a 2008 book by New York Times perfume critic Chandler Burr called The Perfect Scent: A Year Behind the Scenes of the Perfume Industry in Paris and New York."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Sarah_Jessica_Parker_Lovely_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Sarah_Jessica_Parker_Lovely_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lovely_(perfume)","wikidata":"Q55621366"},{"title":"Lavandula","blocks":[{"text":"Lavandula is a genus of 47 known species of perennial flowering plants in the sage family, Lamiaceae. It is native to regions of the Iberian Peninsula and Mediterranean coastline, the Middle East, extending to the Indian subcontinent."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/Single_lavender_flower02.jpg/330px-Single_lavender_flower02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumb